feat(customer-detail): Customer Heartbeat strip — render the relationship

Product Director's #4 board recommendation: "show Felipe his real fans
at a glance." Replaces the cold contact-card vibe with a visible signal
strip on every customer profile.

components/app/CustomerHeartbeat.tsx — pure presentational component.
Four binary signals (not a percentile, not a 0-100 score):
  - Active plan        → has plan_subscriptions row with status='active'
  - Recent visit       → ≥1 schedule_items row in last 90 days
  - Quote engaged      → ≥1 proposal where status≥sent
  - 6+ months on book  → acquired_at older than 180 days

Each signal renders as a small pulse + an icon + a one-line "what it
means today." Aggregate score (0-4) sets the heading: Strong / Warm /
Cool / New-or-dormant. Top dot animate-pulses when the relationship is
strong; goes quiet otherwise. The point is operator empathy: Felipe
opens a customer card and immediately knows whether to call them today
or schedule a referral ask.

Wired into app/(authed)/customers/[id]/page.tsx:
- New proposalsRes query in the parallel Promise.all (one extra round-
  trip; 5 queries instead of 4)
- Heartbeat signals computed inline from the existing visits + subRes +
  proposals + customer.acquired_at (no new schema)
- Renders as the first card in the right-column rail, above Property,
  Notes, etc.

